    {
        "id": "en:word:however",
        "label": "however",
        "fields": {
            "part_of_speech": "adverb",
            "pronunciation": ["/haʊˈevə/"],
            "audio": "audio/a9ef6fb4add74a0f599006a82d307fae3d8a11a47157e61f73a0f7790e76acfa.wav",
            "reference_images": [
                "images/8d8087c2dea95b48c69b17f573e4aa775530af006048c7789044d28e30edd138.jpg"
            ],
            "usage_notes": {
                "en": "However introduces a contrast between statements. Example: It was sunny. However, it started to rain. The two picnic scenes support the change; however is not a name for rain.",
                "de": "However leitet einen Gegensatz zwischen Aussagen ein. „It was sunny. However, it started to rain.“ = Es war sonnig. Allerdings fing es an zu regnen. Die Picknickszenen zeigen den Wechsel; however bedeutet nicht Regen.",
                "id": "However memperkenalkan pertentangan antara pernyataan. “It was sunny. However, it started to rain.” = Cuacanya cerah. Namun, hujan mulai turun. Dua adegan piknik mendukung perubahan ini; however bukan nama untuk hujan.",
                "ja": "howeverは文と文の対比を示します。「It was sunny. However, it started to rain.」＝晴れていました。しかし、雨が降り始めました。二つのピクニック場面は変化の手がかりで、however自体が雨を指すわけではありません。"
            }
        },
        "class": "lexical:adverb",
        "tags": ["adverb", "beginner", "sentence-structure"],
